@page "/notifications"
@attribute [Authorize]

@*
    Standalone notification inbox for vendors and crew — every notification
    across every event they're on, newest first.

    This is also the landing page for the deep link in the WhatsApp message
    (/notifications?id={announcementId}), which is why it reads the id from
    the query string and passes it through as HighlightId: arriving from
    WhatsApp should drop you straight onto the expanded message with its
    attachment links, not a list you have to search.
*@

<div class="p-5 md:p-8 space-y-5 max-w-4xl">
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-800">Notifications</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
            Updates from the Admin/Manager team for the events you're assigned to. Attachments open as links.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* Put first on purpose: someone who came here wondering why they missed a
       shift alert should meet the switch that fixes it before the list of things
       they already missed. *@
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm p-5">
        <PushNotificationSettings />
    </div>

    @* Two distinct feeds, deliberately not merged. Announcements are messages a
       human composed and broadcast; Activity is generated by business events and
       also went out over email and WhatsApp. Interleaving them would hide a
       cancellation among newsletters and blur who actually said what. *@
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm p-5">
        <PlatformNotificationsPanel />
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm p-5">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mb-1">Announcements</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">Messages from the Admin/Manager team.</p>
        <EventNotificationsPanel InboxMode="true" ShowEventTitle="true" HighlightId="@_highlightId" />
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // Same [SupplyParameterFromQuery] approach the Login pages use for
    // ReturnUrl — the framework binds ?id=… straight onto this property.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "id")] public Guid? Id { get; set; }

    private Guid? _highlightId => Id;
}
